    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n****VIRTUAL TOUR AVAILABLE****\n\nNestled on a quiet residential road in the highly sought-after Glenascaul area of Oranmore, 'Amberly' is a beautifully upgraded family home offering the perfect balance of comfort, energy efficiency, and convenience. Extensively renovated in 2011, the property has been thoughtfully modernised to create a bright, spacious, and practical home.\n\nExceptional energy-saving features include triple-glazed windows, composite front and rear doors, external insulation, a heat recovery ventilation system, and Thermasol solar panels providing hot water. The converted attic adds two versatile rooms and an ensuite, while strategically placed Velux windows enhance natural light throughout the home. A cosy solid fuel stove complements the zoned Firebird oil-fired heating system, ensuring warmth and comfort all year round. French doors open from the living space onto a private side garden, creating an ideal setting for outdoor dining and family enjoyment.\n\nIdeally located just minutes from Oranmore Village, the property enjoys easy access to an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools, shops, cafés, restaurants, sporting facilities, and every essential amenity. It is perfectly positioned for commuters, with immediate access to the M6 and M18 motorways, Galway City, and the major multinational employers located in Parkmore, Ballybrit, and the wider Galway business hubs. This is an outstanding opportunity to acquire a turnkey family home in one of Oranmore's most desirable residential locations.\n\nDNG Leonard & Heaslip for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of the property whose Agents they are, give notice that: (i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not constitute part of, an offer or contract. (ii) Any intending purchasers or tenants must not rely the descriptions, dimensions, references to condition or necessary permissions for use and occupation as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. (iii) No person in the employment of DNG Leonard & Heaslip has any authority to make or give representation or warranty whatever in relation to this development. DNG Leonard & Heaslip accept no liability (including liability to any prospective purchaser or lessee by reason of negligence or negligent misstatement) for loss or damage caused by any statements, opinions, information or other matters (expressed or implied) arising out of, contained in or derived from, or for any omissions from this brochure."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.9 x 1.8\nWide entrace hall with tiled flooring.\n\nKitchen - 5.2 x 6.3\nSpacious open plan kitchen with tiled flooring, built in kitchen units with granite counter tops , island feature, side window, door to back garden and velux window.\n\nLiving Room - 3.7 x 4.5\nCozy front facing living room with open fire place with stove insert and front and side windows.\n\nUtility Room - 2.6 x 2.3\nRear facing with tiled floor, back door and built in units with granite counter tops.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 3.8 x 3.9\nLarge front facing double room with two windows, built in wardrobe and laminate flooring.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.6 x 4.5\nLarge front facing double room with laminate flooring.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.7 x 4.3\nRear facing double room with laminate flooring.\n\nBathroom - 3.2 x 3.7\nLarge bathroom with tiled floor, whb, wc and shower.\n\nBedroom Four - 3.6x3.2\nWith laminate flooring, velux window and storage.\n\nBedroom Five - 5.8 x 3.2\nWith laminate flooring, 2 velux windows and storage.\n\nEn Suite - 2.3 x 3.1\nWith tiled floor and velux window.\n\n"
